<h1>The Four-Part Prompt Framework</h1>

<p>AI pays attention to four things in a prompt:</p>

<p style="margin: 0 0 8px 0;">• The <b>Task</b> (what to build)</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 8px 0;">• The <b>Context</b> (who it's for or what it's about)</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 8px 0;">• The <b>Tone/Format</b> (the style or feel)</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• The <b>Details</b> (specific content to include)</p>

<div style="display: flex; gap: 12px; margin: 20px 0; flex-wrap: wrap;">
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 100px; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px; text-align: center;">
    <div style="font-size: 30px; margin-bottom: 6px;">📋</div>
    <p style="font-weight: bold; color: #1F1976; margin: 0; font-size: 13px;">Task</p>
  </div>
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 100px; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px; text-align: center;">
    <div style="font-size: 30px; margin-bottom: 6px;">🎯</div>
    <p style="font-weight: bold; color: #1F1976; margin: 0; font-size: 13px;">Context</p>
  </div>
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 100px; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px; text-align: center;">
    <div style="font-size: 30px; margin-bottom: 6px;">🎨</div>
    <p style="font-weight: bold; color: #1F1976; margin: 0; font-size: 13px;">Tone/Format</p>
  </div>
  <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 100px; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px; text-align: center;">
    <div style="font-size: 30px; margin-bottom: 6px;">🔍</div>
    <p style="font-weight: bold; color: #1F1976; margin: 0; font-size: 13px;">Details</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>A strong prompt hits all four. A generic-looking result is almost always missing one of them, not a sign the AI misunderstood or isn't capable.</p>

<p>That reframe matters for how you coach students through the AI Design Challenges. When a page comes back bland, the fix usually isn't "try again," it's figuring out which of the four pieces to add.</p>

